&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Product&amp;nbsp; - Connect Platform&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Connect is Stripe’s platform for businesses that serve other businesses. It gives platforms the infrastructure to represent the people and companies in their ecosystem, onboard and verify them, manage their accounts, accept payments, and pay them out - without building payments, compliance, or financial-services systems themselves. This is how businesses like Shopify can help entrepreneurs run and grow their businesses. It is also the kind of infrastructure that marketplaces such as DoorDash need to coordinate money movement across large networks of restaurants, merchants, and dashers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Connect has impact across industries. &lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.com/customers/shopify&quot;&gt;Shopify&lt;/a&gt; uses Stripe to embed financial services for merchants; &lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.com/customers/lugg&quot;&gt;Lugg&lt;/a&gt; streamlines worker onboarding and offers instant payouts; &lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.com/customers/doorloop&quot;&gt;DoorLoop&lt;/a&gt; reduces manual customer onboarding tasks by nearly 50% with Stripe; and &lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.com/customers/sharetribe&quot;&gt;Sharetribe&lt;/a&gt; helps entrepreneurs launch and run marketplaces on Stripe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;AI is accelerating the emergence of entirely new business models: global networks of creators and experts, AI-native marketplaces, and agent-driven products that change how people discover, buy, sell, and deliver services. These businesses are more dynamic than traditional platforms: participants may operate across borders, take on different roles, and need new ways to establish trust, access financial capabilities, and get paid.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Connect Abstractions team owns the platform primitives that make these models possible. We are building the foundational abstractions for representing participants, onboarding them safely, configuring their capabilities, and managing their lifecycle on Stripe. Our work will determine how quickly the next generation of platforms can launch, how flexibly they can evolve, and how much of Stripe they can bring to the businesses and people they serve.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why this role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a chance to define a foundational product area at Stripe. You will turn a fast-changing set of user and product needs into durable platform primitives that work across products, industries, and geographies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The role combines high-leverage strategy with hands-on product execution. You will work through ambiguous, consequential questions like: what should a platform be able to model? What should be simple by default but flexible when needed? How can Stripe make complex financial infrastructure feel effortless for a platform and its users?&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The outcome of your work will compound. The abstractions you help create will be reused across Connect and Stripe, shaping what new products platforms can build and how quickly they can bring them to market.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for an entrepreneurial Product Manager to build the platform experiences behind Connect&#39;s next generation of users. You will own critical product primitives that platforms, including the fastest-growing AI companies, use to onboard, configure, and manage their users on Stripe. You will turn a clear strategic direction into products that solve hard user problems today while creating a coherent, extensible foundation for business models that are still being invented.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is for someone who enjoys the depth of platform work but is uncompromising about product craft and solving real user needs - both the ones users have today and will have in the future. The work is not building infra for its own sake; you will build capabilities that help our users launch a new marketplace, enable a global network to pay its contributors, or give a business entirely new ways for their end users to earn.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring the next generation of Connect accounts to life. Own key product areas within the account platform, translating strategy into a focused roadmap, crisp product decisions, and high-quality launches.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build from use cases. Start with the real problems platforms face, such as onboarding a new seller, supporting a complex business model, or evolving a user&#39;s financial capabilities, and then work towards the primitives needed to solve them well.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make sophisticated infrastructure feel simple. Partner with engineering and design to create API and product experiences that are powerful and intuitive.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;See around corners. Develop a strong point of view on how AI will change platform economics, participant models, and financial workflows. Make focused foundational investments that unlock the next wave of demand.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn user signals into durable product investments. Work closely with users, Sales, Partnerships, and other Stripe teams to distinguish bespoke requests from patterns that should become scalable platform capabilities, connecting business needs, user needs, and platform evolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive high-velocity, high-craft execution and own outcomes. Lead cross-functional work from discovery through launch, and hold yourself accountable for developer experience, platform adoption, user value, and business impact, not simply features shipped.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are a product builder who can move easily between a user’s hardest problem, the business opportunity behind it, and the product decisions needed to solve it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have worked on technically complex products - such as APIs, developer tools, shared platform capabilities, or core product experiences - but you do not build tech/platform for its own sake. You see strong platform design as a way to help users move faster, create better products, and unlock new business models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are opinionated, thoughtful, and execution-oriented. You can focus a team on the few decisions that matter most, create momentum in ambiguous situations, and ship products that raise the bar for both quality and impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of product management experience, with meaningful time owning platform, API, or developer-facing products end to end&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to own a product area end to end: setting strategy, driving execution, and measuring outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical instincts and comfort defining the measurement framework before you ship&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear written communication and the ability to build alignment across functions and levels&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in payments, fintech, or financial infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience productizing bespoke or custom solutions into broadly available platform capabilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of making well-judged foundational investments ahead of user demand&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;From Fivetran’s founding until now, our mission has remained the same: to make access to data as simple and reliable as electricity. With Fivetran, customer data arrives in their warehouses, canonical and ready to query, with no engineering or maintenance required. We’re proud that more organizations continue to leverage our technology every day to become truly data-driven.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fivetran and dbt Labs are bringing together two industry-leading companies with a shared mission: helping organizations unlock the full value of their data.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Together, we’re delivering the data infrastructure layer that helps organizations move, transform, and trust their data — from the moment data moves, through every transformation, to the context teams and AI systems rely on.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fivetran helps organizations automate data movement across the systems, clouds, engines, and tools they rely on. dbt Labs pioneered analytics engineering, helping teams transform data into reliable, governed insights. Together, we support thousands of organizations as they build a trusted foundation for analytics, AI, and better business decisions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As we bring our teams and technology together, we’re building on the strengths of both companies while continuing to deliver the products and experiences our customers know and trust. It’s an exciting time to join us: we’re creating a company with the scale, talent, and technology to help more organizations put their data to work with greater speed, confidence, and impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;During this transition period, you may see references to both Fivetran and dbt Labs throughout our recruiting process as we integrate our teams, systems, and career sites.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a member of the COO Office you will be responsible for defining how the combined Fivetran + dbt Labs organization uses its core collaborative platforms to get work done.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As we bring two companies together, we inherit two sets of tooling conventions across every major platform — with no single owner responsible for defining a consistent, governed baseline. This role owns that mandate. The majority of the work centers on making Notion excellent as NewCo’s primary knowledge management platform: workspace governance, information architecture, content standards, and page ownership. Beyond Notion, the role publishes and maintains best-practice guidance for Slack, Google Workspace, and Jira, and partners with department champions to drive adoption across the company.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role also leverages AI to manage these systems — keeping workspaces clean, enforcing best practices, and partnering with the AI Transformation team to align on how we use AI within these tools.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a full-time position based out of our &lt;strong&gt;Denver&lt;/strong&gt; office. Our hybrid work model offers a blend of remote flexibility and in-person collaboration, including two days in the office each week to connect and build as a team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Define and drive NewCo’s ways of working across six dimensions:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;How we collaborate internally — set standards for how teams work together inside Notion, Slack, and Google Workspace&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;How we collaborate externally — extend that guidance to shared spaces with partners, customers, and vendors, outlining what should differ from our internal norms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;How we make decisions — establish lightweight, documented decision-making practices (e.g. DACI-style ownership)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;How we document — own Notion governance, information architecture, and content standards so our knowledge base is a trusted source of truth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;How we project manage — set shared baselines for Jira project and program structure, naming, and usage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;How we communicate — define Slack conventions, channel governance, and async norms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Alongside these:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define what “good” looks like for each core tool and publish it as canonical, company-wide guidance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage AI to keep workspaces clean, audit for inconsistencies, and maintain standards at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run recurring compliance checks and drive channels and workspaces into conformance over time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with department champions to roll out standards and support adoption&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Align with the AI Transformation team on how we apply AI within these tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Incorporate ongoing employee-experience feedback from the People team to refine standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide executional support for COO Office communications, in coordination with the Head of Internal Communications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills We’re Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep, hands-on expertise administering Notion at scale — governance, databases, information architecture, and permissions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong working command of Slack, Google Workspace, and Jira administration and best practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to define standards and drive cross-functional adoption without direct authority&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written communication — able to produce clear, canonical guidance that teams actually follow&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Program management discipline: can run rollouts, track compliance, and manage stakeholders across functions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort operating in ambiguity and building a function from the ground up&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong judgment on where to standardize vs. where to leave teams autonomy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required AI Competencies&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced fluency with conversational AI systems (Claude, ChatGPT) — not just basic prompting, but structuring complex, multi-step work and reliably getting high-quality output&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated track record of redesigning workflows around AI, not merely bolting it onto existing processes — able to identify where AI creates real leverage and where it doesn’t&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with AI features native to our core tools (e.g. Notion AI, Glean-style search, Atlassian Intelligence) and the judgment to codify their use into company best practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to build AI-assisted governance at scale — using AI to audit workspaces, surface inconsistencies, and maintain standards across thousands of pages and channels&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency with AI agents and automation to eliminate manual, repetitive administration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience standing up tooling governance during a merger, acquisition, or major org integration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Notion certification or comparable demonstrated platform mastery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building AI-driven internal tools, automations, or agents&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with change management frameworks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-Hybrid #LI-SR1&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;The compensation range displayed on this job posting reflects the minimum and maximum target for new hire compensation for the target position and level, and may include sales incentives or target bonuses depending on the role. &amp;nbsp;Our compensation ranges are determined by role, level, and location. Our job titles may span more than one career level. Within the range, individual compensation is determined by additional factors, including job-related skills, experience, relevant education or training, business need, market demands. The compensation range is subject to change and may be modified in the future. Your recruiter can share more about the specific compensation range for your location during the hiring process.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Denver Pay Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$144,689.50&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$180,861.50 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p-rich_text_section&quot; style=&quot;line-height: 1.3;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Perks and Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;100% employer-paid medical insurance&lt;strong&gt;*&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous paid time-off policy (PTO), plus paid sick time, inclusive parental leave policy, holidays, and volunteer days off&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;RSU stock grants*&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional development and training opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Company virtual happy hours, free food, and fun team-building activities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monthly cell phone stipend&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Access to an innovative mental health support platform that offers personalized care and resources in areas such as: therapy, coaching, and self-guided mindfulness exercises for all covered employees and their covered dependents.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.3;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;*&lt;/strong&gt;May vary by country and worker type - please reach out to your recruiter for more information&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.3;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Click &lt;a href=&quot;https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1CdawUwjo1Q1B7ghZJ_owdmmHB8VtqhBu?usp=sharing&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt; to learn more about Fivetran&#39;s Benefits by Region.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.3;&quot;&gt;We’re honored to be &lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;https://fivetran.com/blog/hvr-acquisition-series-d&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://fivetran.com/blog/hvr-acquisition-series-d&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;valued at over $5.6 billion&lt;/a&gt;, but more importantly, we’re proud of our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;https://fivetran.com/culture&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://fivetran.com/culture&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;core values of Get Stuck In, Do the Right Thing, and One Team, One Dream&lt;/a&gt;. Read about us in&amp;nbsp;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;https://fivetran-com.s3.amazonaws.com/news/forbes-aug-sept-2022-digital-reprint-10-21-22.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://fivetran-com.s3.amazonaws.com/news/forbes-aug-sept-2022-digital-reprint-10-21-22.pdf&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;Forbes&lt;/a&gt;.&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.3;&quot;&gt;Fivetran brings together high-quality talent across the globe to make data access as easy and reliable as electricity for our customers. We value and recognize that our customers benefit from having innovative teams made of people from many backgrounds, experiences, and identities. Fivetran promotes diversity, equity, inclusion &amp;amp; belonging through attracting, recruiting, developing, and retaining a diverse workforce, not only because it is the right thing to do, but because it helps us build a world-class company to better serve our customers, our people and our communities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.3;&quot;&gt;To learn more about Fivetran’s culture and what it’s like to be part of the team, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xlhtp4dGh8o&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;click here&lt;/a&gt; and enjoy our video.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.3;&quot;&gt;To learn more about our candidate privacy policy, you can &lt;a href=&quot;https://fivetran.com/candidate-privacy&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;read our statement here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.3;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;We are committed to ensuring that all candidates have an equal opportunity to participate in our interview process. If you require accommodations at any stage of the process due to a disability, medical condition, or any other circumstance, please don&#39;t hesitate to submit your request by filling out this &lt;a href=&quot;https://forms.gle/V7k3t4u9j523XkEt6&quot;&gt;form&lt;/a&gt;. We will work with you to provide reasonable accommodations to facilitate your participation and ensure a fair and accessible interview experience. Your request and any information provided will be kept confidential and will not impact your candidacy. We look forward to hearing from you and accommodating your needs to the best of our ability.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Scale has been the leading AI data foundry, helping fuel the most exciting advancements in AI, including frontier model training, enterprise adoption, defense applications, and autonomous vehicles. Our mission is to develop reliable AI systems for the world&#39;s most important decisions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Coding is one of Scale&#39;s strongest and fastest-moving domains. We built&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;SWE-Bench Pro&lt;/strong&gt;, a contamination-resistant benchmark of 1,865 long-horizon software engineering tasks across 41 repositories — including a first-of-its-kind private set drawn from proprietary startup codebases — which cut frontier model scores from over 70% on SWE-Bench Verified to roughly 23%, and became a reference point for how the industry measures coding agents. We then extended that foundation with &lt;strong&gt;SWE Atlas&lt;/strong&gt;, an evaluation suite spanning Codebase QnA, Test Writing, and Refactoring, which measures the full engineering loop rather than issue resolution alone. And we are among the largest external contributors to the &lt;strong&gt;FrontierBench&lt;/strong&gt; (Formerly Terminal-Bench&lt;strong&gt;)&lt;/strong&gt; lineage, contributing more tasks than any other single organization to the launch set.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Senior AI Product Manager&lt;/strong&gt; to own and scale this &lt;strong&gt;Coding&lt;/strong&gt; portfolio from here. In this role, you will define the strategy, roadmap, and operational excellence of Scale&#39;s coding data products, RL environments, and agentic coding evaluations. You will work across AI Product Management, ML Researchers, Engineering, Operations, and Go-To-Market teams to turn our benchmark credibility into a durable, revenue-generating product line that leading labs depend on to train the next generation of software engineering agents.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will serve as the product owner for coding initiatives, driving task design, environment infrastructure, expert contributor quality, customer adoption, and business impact. You will work directly with leading AI labs and enterprise customers, representing Scale as a thought partner in how coding models are trained and measured.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate combines strong product judgment, hands-on technical depth in software engineering, operational rigor, and customer-facing experience, with a passion for turning emerging model capabilities into scalable data products.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You Will&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the roadmap and strategy for Scale&#39;s Coding portfolio, defining priorities across SFT and preference data, reinforcement learning environments, agentic task suites, and evaluation products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extend the SWE-Bench Pro and SWE Atlas franchises; deciding what comes next as agents saturate current tasks, and converting benchmark authority into training-data and environment revenue.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Facilitate exploration of the Coding domain and drive alignment among AI-PM, ML, Engineering, Operations, and GTM stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate, prioritize, and operationalize new coding product proposals, ensuring alignment with customer demand, model capability frontiers, and company strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and manage the end-to-end coding product lifecycle, from ideation and task taxonomy design to pilot, launch, scaling, and sunset decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with ML researchers and senior software engineers to develop trustworthy task specifications, rubric and grader design, verifiable reward signals, and quality bars for code correctness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive the roadmap for coding infrastructure; Harbor-native container environments, execution sandboxes, reproducible repo images, automated verification, and contributor tooling — to improve scalability, reduce manual effort, and accelerate delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish governance processes for data quality, contamination and leakage prevention, license and IP hygiene, reproducibility, auditability, and release management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Grow and steward the expert contributor network of professional software engineers across languages, frameworks, and seniority levels, balancing throughput, cost, and quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and grow external partnerships across the coding ecosystem, including open-source benchmark collaborations, enterprise codebase partnerships, and joint releases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work directly with frontier AI labs and enterprise customers to understand where their coding models fail, gather feedback, and influence future investments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track adoption, usage, model-impact signals, and business outcomes, using data-driven insights to guide roadmap decisions and resource allocation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify new coding capability areas; long-horizon agentic work, repo-scale refactoring, debugging, code review, migrations, low-resource languages; that strengthen Scale&#39;s leadership and create new revenue opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with GTM teams to support customer engagements, thought leadership initiatives, product launches, and strategic partnerships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ideally, You&#39;d Have&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in product management, technical program management, consulting, or customer-facing technical roles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical depth in software engineering; you can read code, reason about a codebase, and hold your own with senior engineers and ML researchers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with how coding models are trained and evaluated, including post-training methods, agentic scaffolds and harnesses, and coding benchmarks such as SWE-Bench and Terminal-Bench.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building and scaling products that require coordination across engineering, operations, and business teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent stakeholder management and executive communication skills, with a demonstrated ability to drive alignment across cross-functional organizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical skills and the ability to translate ambiguous market and customer signals into clear product strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with AI researchers, ML teams, developer tools, or human-in-the-loop data pipelines is strongly preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Entrepreneurial mindset with a track record of creating new products, programs, or business initiatives from the ground up.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bias for action and comfort operating in fast-moving, ambiguous environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion for advancing AI coding capability and helping define how the industry builds and measures software engineering agents.&lt;/li&gt;
